course: dictionary
lesson: 6960
title: Words from a funeral
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pallbearer is one of the people who carry the coffin at a funeral. You can work out much of the meaning from the word's parts. Pall is the cloth that covers a coffin, and bearer means someone who carries something.
explain: Context gives more clues. «Pallbearers carry the coffin; they may be family, friends or people who work for the funeral director.» The sentence tells you the job is carrying the coffin, and it tells you who might do it. Swap in your meaning: "People who carry the coffin carry the coffin." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Some pallbearers walk beside the coffin as an honour, even when they do not carry it. Carrying the coffin is a sign of love and respect for the person who has died. Often there are six pallbearers, but the number can vary.
fact: A pallbearer is one of the people who carries the coffin at a funeral.
fact: A pallbearer can also be a person who walks beside the coffin as an honour.
fact: The pall is the cloth that covers a coffin.
fact: Pallbearers are usually family members or close friends of the person who died.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they often give you its meaning.
exercise: «Pallbearers carry the coffin; they may be family, friends or people who work for the funeral director.» Who may be a pallbearer? | Only children | *Family, friends or people who work for the funeral director | The person who is being buried | A stranger who sells ice cream
exercise: In the word pallbearer, what does pall mean? | *The cloth that covers a coffin | A kind of bread | A small bird | A heavy stone
exercise: What is a pallbearer? | A person who sings at a wedding | A person who writes the names on the gravestone | The driver of the funeral car | *One of the people who carry the coffin at a funeral
test: Carrying the coffin is a sign of what? | Boredom and tiredness | *Love and respect | Surprise and excitement | Anger and fear
test: Why are pallbearers usually family or close friends? | Because they are the tallest people there | *Because carrying the coffin is an honour shown out of love and respect | Because they are paid to sing | Because they are the youngest people at the funeral
exam: Using the word parts and the context, what does pallbearer mean? | A person who arranges the flowers at a church | *One of the people who carry the coffin at a funeral, or who walks beside it as an honour | A guest who reads a poem aloud | A person who drives the hearse
